/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 130 0 R
/T (This project successfully demonstrates a proactive safety mechanism that eliminates standby high-voltage potential on open power sockets. By combining optocoupler-based low-voltage detection with continuous shunt resistor current monitoring, the circuit achieves reliable automatic power delivery only when a genuine load is connected. The system significantly reduces electrocution risks compared to conventional passive socket covers or reactive fault interrupters, offering a robust foundation for next-generation smart outlet safety.)
/E (This project successfully demonstrates a proactive safety mechanism that eliminates standby high-voltage potential on open power sockets. By combining optocoupler-based low-voltage detection with continuous shunt resistor current monitoring, the circuit achieves reliable automatic power delivery only when a genuine load is connected. The system significantly reduces electrocution risks compared to conventional passive socket covers or reactive fault interrupters, offering a robust foundation for next-generation smart outlet safety.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
