636 0 obj
<<
/Title (This project presents a Smart Shock Protection & Auto-Sensing Outlet that keeps the socket completely de-energized from high-voltage mains during standby. The circuit utilizes a low-voltage \(5V DC\) sensing loop featuring an optocoupler to detect when a physical load is connected. Upon detection, an Arduino triggers a relay to switch the socket to 230V AC mains. While active, the system monitors AC current via a low-value shunt sensing resistor connected to an analog pin. When the load is disconnected, the system instantly cuts the 230V AC supply and reverts the socket back to safe 5V DC standby mode.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 577 0 R
/Prev 648 0 R
/Next 613 0 R
>>
endobj
